; ============================================================================
; ten-fifty5.com — TARGET zone for Cloudflare (Wix decommission, phase 1)
;
; This file IS the target state, not a copy of the Wix zone: the Wix-only
; records (s1/s2/sel1._domainkey, sg, en, and the _dmarc CNAME) are
; deliberately absent, and _dmarc is re-issued below as our own TXT.
;
; Import:  Cloudflare -> the zone -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export
;          -> Import DNS records -> upload this file.
; Then:    set every record to DNS only (grey cloud). Render fronts its own
;          TLS; proxying on top of it is not wanted here.
;
; Values transcribed from the Wix panel 2026-08-22 and each confirmed to
; resolve. Do not retype the DKIM tokens by hand — that is why this file
; exists.
; ============================================================================

$ORIGIN ten-fifty5.com.
$TTL 3600

; --- APEX -------------------------------------------------------------------
; RESOLVED 2026-08-22 — the precondition this block described is now met.
; ten-fifty5.com is a custom domain on the Render locker-room service, set to
; redirect to www, and Render issued its certificate the same day (valid to
; 2026-11-20). The value below is Render's, not a guess: it is what the
; authoritative Wix nameservers now return, and what nextpointtennis.com's
; working apex resolves to.
;
; The three Wix parking A records (185.230.63.x) that used to sit here were
; serving a certificate that EXPIRED 2026-08-16, so for six days the bare
; domain gave every visitor a browser security warning. They have been deleted
; at Wix. Do not reinstate them, and do not leave this apex out of the
; Cloudflare zone: without this line the bare domain simply stops existing at
; cutover, which is the same outage wearing a different hat.
;
; Target behaviour: apex -> Render -> 301 to www, with a Render-issued cert.
@                       1800 IN A     216.24.57.1

; --- WEB --------------------------------------------------------------------
www                     3600 IN CNAME locker-room-26kd.onrender.com.

; --- CLERK (login + Clerk's own outbound mail) ------------------------------
clerk                   3600 IN CNAME frontend-api.clerk.services.
accounts                3600 IN CNAME accounts.clerk.services.
clkmail                 3600 IN CNAME mail.c608ch2ifwtk.clerk.services.
clk._domainkey          3600 IN CNAME dkim1.c608ch2ifwtk.clerk.services.
clk2._domainkey         3600 IN CNAME dkim2.c608ch2ifwtk.clerk.services.

; --- AMAZON SES (transactional mail) ----------------------------------------
; These three also carry NextPoint's booking confirmations, invoices and
; receipts, which send from noreply@ten-fifty5.com. Losing one degrades
; deliverability for BOTH brands, quietly.
imwkcbcr2kzvwv3phgsf5ynvojuhucoh._domainkey 3600 IN CNAME imwkcbcr2kzvwv3phgsf5ynvojuhucoh.dkim.amazonses.com.
r3o5cfok7zeldlj6hr7d3e4efsubk35p._domainkey 3600 IN CNAME r3o5cfok7zeldlj6hr7d3e4efsubk35p.dkim.amazonses.com.
tirvfmypxsmpeziylont7wtg67tlwa4s._domainkey 3600 IN CNAME tirvfmypxsmpeziylont7wtg67tlwa4s.dkim.amazonses.com.

; --- KLAVIYO (marketing email sending domain) -------------------------------
; Added 2026-08-30, mirroring nextpointtennis.com. Klaviyo had NO authenticated
; sending domain on EITHER brand, so marketing mail left as info@ten-fifty5.com
; signed on Klaviyo's SHARED infrastructure and DMARC alignment failed on every
; campaign. p=none meant nothing was blocked - it just pushed mail toward
; Promotions/spam with no error anywhere.
; SUBDOMAIN, not apex: DMARC relaxed alignment accepts a subdomain of the From
; domain, so these align without touching the apex SPF (Google) or the three SES
; DKIM CNAMEs above, which carry transactional mail and must not be disturbed.
; Routing type STATIC, not Klaviyo's recommended "dynamic": dynamic delegates NS
; for this subdomain to Klaviyo and puts it outside this version-controlled zone.
; The klaviyo-site-verification TXT was already present below and is already live.
email                   3600 IN CNAME 3839852462349830343.klaviyodns.com.
km1._domainkey          3600 IN CNAME km1._domainkey.3839852462349830343.klaviyodns.com.
km2._domainkey          3600 IN CNAME km2._domainkey.3839852462349830343.klaviyodns.com.

; --- MAIL -------------------------------------------------------------------
@                       3600 IN MX 10 aspmx.l.google.com.

; --- TXT --------------------------------------------------------------------
; SPF lists Google but not SES on purpose: SES sends with its own envelope
; sender, so it passes SPF on Amazon's domain and aligns DMARC via the three
; DKIM keys above. Do not "fix" this record.
@                       3600 IN TXT "v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all"
@                       3600 IN TXT "google-site-verification=wozW81IucSQPndvD6GbrMA-MBYBLjCFQQAmAnXKqZ3k"
@                       3600 IN TXT "MS=3C4E3C3BE41AD5031BEC6B43872D39B78385438F"
@                       3600 IN TXT "klaviyo-site-verification=RTukzx"

; Replaces the Wix-hosted _dmarc CNAME. Same policy (p=none), reports to us.
_dmarc                  3600 IN TXT "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:info@ten-fifty5.com"
